# Close a race in openrazer's shipped /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-razer.rules.
#
# Upstream acts only on ACTION=="add", and razer_mount guards its
# `chgrp -R plugdev` behind `[ -d /sys/bus/hid/drivers/$DRIVER/$DEVICE_ID ]`.
# For a hid interface the "add" uevent can fire before the razer* driver has
# finished binding and creating its sysfs attributes, so that test fails, the
# chgrp is skipped, and the node is left root:root. openrazer-daemon then
# refuses the device with
#   CRITICAL | Could not access .../device_type, file is not owned by plugdev
# and it silently vanishes from the DBus device list -- razerdash reports
# "no device matching 'BlackWidow V4'" and idles.
#
# The "bind" uevent fires *after* the driver has attached and populated sysfs,
# which is exactly when the group change needs to happen. This rule adds to the
# shipped one rather than replacing it; on a boot that wins the original race
# the chgrp simply runs twice, which is harmless.
ACTION=="bind", SUBSYSTEM=="hid", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1532", \
    RUN+="/bin/sh -c '/usr/bin/chgrp -R plugdev /sys%p || true'"
